const e="4h-county-fair-judging",d=2026,t="Read from the Nebraska 4-H Fairbook (State Fair) General Rules & Information page (2026) and the Gage County Fairbook Clover Kids page (2026), the two pages named by the template's Evidence. The fairbook's Contests, Live Animals and Static Exhibits sub-pages (per-contest and per-species rules) were not part of the Evidence and are not captured. Captured: eligibility and age divisions, entry procedure and deadline, protest process, ribbon meanings, fees, static, contest and livestock rules, on-grounds rules, Clover Kids rules, class list, dates and shows. Not printed, so left empty: Champion and Reserve Champion rules and any points (the template's Champion, Reserve Champion and ribbon points are not in these pages), marks for Public Speaking and Demonstration, rules of the Judging Team Contest, the State Fair venue street address and dates (they are on the Master 4-H Schedule), contact phone and e-mail. The Clover Kids dates and class numbers are those of one county (Gage County) for 2026.",o=JSON.parse('{"Title":"Rules & Criteria","Subtitle":"Nebraska 4-H county and State Fair rules, 2026. Read these rules before you enter.","NoticeTitle":"Please Read Before Entering","Notice":"Youth must be enrolled in 4-H by {{EnrollmentDeadline}}. State Fair animal entries, in-person events and contests are entered online by the 4-H family in ShoWorks by {{StateEntryDeadline}}. Static entries are entered by 4-H staff. A static exhibit must have won a purple ribbon at the county fair to go to the State Fair. Clover Kids (ages 5 to 7) is not a competition and is not eligible for the State Fair.","Notes":["Contest entry fee: {{ContestEntryFee}}. Livestock entry fees: {{LivestockEntryFees}}.","All entry fees are non-refundable.","Only one entry per class per exhibitor can be made in static project areas and in contests.","In-person event exhibitors wear the T-shirt they are given during presentation and awards. Exhibitors must not wear county identification when they take part in contests or show animals (Fashion Show and Culinary Challenge have their own dress codes).","Protests must be made in writing and signed."],"Sections":[{"Key":"general","Title":"General Rules","Items":["These rules apply to all departments of the 4-H section of the Nebraska State Fair. They are grouped as All, Static, Livestock, Contests and On Grounds. Rules for one department are listed under that department.","The Nebraska 4-H State Fair Management Team meets often to answer and solve 4-H issues and complaints in a way that teaches good character, life skills and positive youth development. It reviews and updates the state fairbooks each year, runs webinars to update staff on changes and publishes newsletters with important information and dates. The current 2025-2026 team members are: {{ManagementTeam}}.","If complaints come up during the Nebraska State Fair, the Management Team and the area superintendent act as the protest review group and decide according to the 4-H State Fairbook.","At the Nebraska State Fair, 4-H exhibits are judged against research-based standards that show the level of performance or quality of work.","4-H exhibits at the Nebraska State Fair are entered and shown at the risk of the 4-H member. Nebraska Extension 4-H Youth Development, with the Nebraska State Fair Board, accepts exhibits and takes due care of them. They cannot take responsibility for loss or damage caused by large crowds, the layout of the buildings where displays are held, and the large number of exhibits. Members with exhibits of great sentimental or money value should think about whether to show them.","A project cannot be shown in both 4-H and FFA at the State Fair.","Exhibitors cannot advertise or sell animals or products at the State Fair.","The Nebraska 4-H Code of Conduct applies to all 4-H staff, volunteers, members and parents or guardians during the Nebraska State Fair.","The respective superintendent decides whether an exhibit entry in their division is eligible. Ineligible items are not judged and are not displayed.","An exhibitor who breaks the rules can lose ribbons and other awards and can be removed from the show."]},{"Key":"eligibility","Title":"Eligibility","Items":["Youth must be enrolled in 4-H by {{EnrollmentDeadline}} of the current year.","Junior division: 4-H ages 8 to 10.","Intermediate division: 4-H ages 11 to 13.","Senior division: 4-H ages 14 to 18.","A 4-H member must be 8 before 1 January of the current year, or turn 9 during the current year.","The last year of eligibility is the calendar year in which the member turns 19.","Clover Kids is for youth who are 5 to 7 years old on 1 January of the current calendar year. Clover Kid exhibitors must be enrolled in a 4-H club or as an individual 4-H member by {{EnrollmentDeadline}}. Enrolment website: {{EnrollmentWebsite}}.","Clover Kid static exhibits are not eligible for any other county competition and are not eligible for the State Fair.","Clover Kids can use livestock from a 4-H member who is already on the grounds. Owning livestock is not required. The Clover Kid must say whose animal they use, or say they are bringing their own."]},{"Key":"registration","Title":"How to Enter","Items":["4-H animal entries (beef, sheep, swine, goats, poultry, rabbits and dogs) are entered by the 4-H family online in ShoWorks. The entry deadline is {{StateEntryDeadline}}.","All in-person events, such as the fashion show and contests, are entered online in ShoWorks by the family. The entry deadline is {{StateEntryDeadline}}.","All static entries are entered by 4-H staff.","Static exhibits are released according to County Extension Staff unless the right papers are submitted. Dates and times are on the Master 4-H Schedule.","Clover Kid static projects (Gage County): bring them on {{CloverKidEntryDay1}} or {{CloverKidEntryDay2}} to the 4-H Building. Each exhibitor can have one exhibit per class and up to 10 exhibits.","Clover Kid livestock, rabbit and poultry entries (Gage County) are entered online by {{CloverKidLivestockDeadline}}.","Clover Kid fashion show entry (Gage County): paper registration form at the Extension Office by {{CloverKidFashionDeadline}}.","Enrolment is through 4hOnline: {{EnrollmentWebsite}}."]},{"Key":"fees","Title":"Fees","Items":["Contest entry fee: {{ContestEntryFee}}. This is for all State Fair Judging Contests, Fashion Shows and Robotics Showcase competitions.","Livestock entry fees: {{LivestockEntryFees}}.","All contest and livestock entry fees are non-refundable."]},{"Key":"dates","Title":"Important Dates","Items":["Enrolment deadline: {{EnrollmentDeadline}}.","State Fair entry deadline for animals, in-person events and contests: {{StateEntryDeadline}}.","Clover Kids static entry (Gage County): {{CloverKidEntryDay1}} or {{CloverKidEntryDay2}}. Exhibits are released on {{CloverKidRelease}}.","Clover Kids livestock, rabbit and poultry online entry deadline (Gage County): {{CloverKidLivestockDeadline}}.","Clover Kids shows (Gage County): {{CloverKidShowDates}}.","Clover Kids contests (Gage County): {{CloverKidContests}}.","The State Fair 4-H dates and times are on the Master 4-H Schedule. The fairbook page does not print them."]},{"Key":"venue","Title":"Venue","Items":["Nebraska State Fair: {{StateFairVenue}}.","Clover Kids (Gage County): {{CountyVenue}}.","An infirmary is open on the Fairgrounds 24 hours a day for exhibitors and visitors for emergency care and first aid."]},{"Key":"points","Title":"Ribbons and Placings","Items":["Purple ribbon: an exhibit of superior quality that met and went beyond all the standards.","Blue ribbon: an above-average exhibit that met almost all the standards in a way that goes beyond the normal level.","Red ribbon: an exhibit of average quality that met most of the standards so that the benchmark was reached but not passed.","White ribbon: an exhibit that did not meet most of the standards.","Clover Kids is not a competition. Each Clover Kid exhibitor receives a Clover Kid ribbon. The learning experience is the main reason for taking part."]},{"Key":"prizes","Title":"Awards, Premiums and T-Shirts","Items":["No special awards are given unless the State Fair 4-H Management Team has approved them.","Premiums in all 4-H classes are paid after all counties have confirmed the official results.","T-shirts are given to all in-person event exhibitors (livestock, fashion show, contests). They are not given to static exhibit exhibitors."]},{"Key":"conduct","Title":"Conduct and On-Grounds Rules","Items":["The T-shirts given to exhibitors must be worn for all in-person event exhibitions, during the presentation and awards.","Exhibitors must not have any county identification on their clothing while they take part in contests or show animals. The exceptions are the Fashion Show and the Culinary Challenge. See the individual guidelines of these events for the dress code.","Smoking is not allowed in any barn, to protect exhibitors and livestock.","The State of Nebraska rules on alcohol use and abuse are enforced.","The 4-H/FFA Exhibit building is closed to the public and locked at 9:00 p.m. Security is provided for livestock barns at all times.","Camping is not allowed in the parking lot.","Take care to avoid flammable materials.","Golf carts and service carts need a permit to run in State Fair Park. See the Nebraska State Fair website for the rules.","The State Fair management works to protect people from injury but is not responsible for any accident, damage or loss. If an accident happens, quick help is available at the First Aid Station. Each person is personally responsible for any injury."]},{"Key":"complaints","Title":"Protests","Items":["The respective superintendent has the power to make decisions based on the 4-H Fairbook. When needed, a committee is set up as a protest review group. It meets when needed.","All protests (other than livestock) must be made in writing and signed, and given to the State Fair Management Team.","A protest must include: names of the people involved; the nature of the concerns; the situation and papers; recommendations to correct it; the specific action or rule in question; other people the committee can contact; and the steps the people involved took before the protest.","The committee reviews the written protest. It can talk to the affected people and to show officials, including Nebraska State Fair management. It makes recommendations and tells the affected group or people, both by mouth and in writing.","While a protest is open, the exhibitor can be allowed to show, but the results of the showing can change after the protest process.","The 4-H State Fair Management Team can withhold any award. The exhibitor can be removed from the show if the action calls for it.","Protests are not accepted after the exhibit is released from the 4-H Division of the State Fair.","Protests about the integrity of judges, decisions, placings or other evaluations are not accepted.","Protests about livestock must follow the process in the State Fair General Livestock Rules & Regulations."]},{"Key":"levels","Title":"County and State","Items":["A static exhibit must have received a purple ribbon at the county fair to go on to the State Fair."]},{"Key":"other","Title":"Exhibit Rules and Other Notes","Items":["Large static exhibits made for outdoors (for example lawn and garden furniture, trailers, animal feeding structures, picnic tables and barn quilts) can be shown outdoors at the choice of 4-H staff or area superintendents if more display space is needed inside the exhibit hall.","No firearms and no items with a blade (broad heads, knives, saws and so on) or related items of any kind can be exhibited. This covers real items, copies of items and item parts. Shooting sports accessories are allowed as set out in the Conservation, Wildlife and Shooting Sports Fairbook.","Copyrighted writing, artwork, videos and images can be used in 4-H educational exhibits under Fair Use for education. To qualify for Fair Use, the 4-H member must: use only a small amount of the copyrighted work; add new meaning to make it original; rework it and use it in a totally different way; and use it for non-profit purposes. Giving credit to the original creator is also recommended.","Clover Kid My Choice exhibits can use any media and should relate to the project area. A Photography Display is up to three 4 inch by 6 inch photos on 11 inch by 14 inch black or white poster board. Posters or drawings are at most 8 1/2 inch by 11 inch.","Clover Kid project descriptions are in The Big Book of 4-H Cloverbud Activities, available at the Extension Office.","For PeeWee Showmanship and PeeWee Exhibits, see the Open Class Fairbook at {{GageFairWebsite}}."]}],"Documents":[{"Title":"Nebraska 4-H Fairbook (State Fair), General Rules & Information","Url":"https://4h.unl.edu/4-h-fairbook-nebraska-state-fair/general-rules-information/"},{"Title":"Gage County Fairbook, Clover Kids","Url":"https://extension.unl.edu/gage-county-fairbook/clover-kids/"},{"Title":"4-H Fairbook (Nebraska State Fair)","Url":"https://4h.unl.edu/4-h-fairbook-nebraska-state-fair/"}]}'),a=[],i=[{AgeGroup:"Clover Kids NC",Source:"Gage County Fairbook, Clover Kids, introduction and Clover Kids rules",Sections:{About:["The Clover Kids program promotes the positive development of youth to become competent, caring and contributing citizens. The learning experience is the main reason for taking part."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Ages 5 to 7 on 1 January of the current calendar year.","Enrolled in a 4-H club or as an individual 4-H member by {{EnrollmentDeadline}}.","Each exhibitor receives a Clover Kid ribbon. This is not a competition.","For more information on contest registration, visit {{ContestsPage}}.","Contests listed for Clover Kids (Gage County, Division 1): K100104 Premier Communication Contest on {{ClKPremierContest}}; K100107 Fashion Show, Purchased or Constructed Garment, on {{ClKFashionShow}}."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:["Each Clover Kid exhibitor receives a Clover Kid ribbon. No premiums are printed."],Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- The Clover Kids program promotes the positive development of youth to become competent, caring and contributing citizens. The learning experience is the main reason for taking part.

## Rules
- Ages 5 to 7 on 1 January of the current calendar year.
- Enrolled in a 4-H club or as an individual 4-H member by {{EnrollmentDeadline}}.
- Each exhibitor receives a Clover Kid ribbon. This is not a competition.
- For more information on contest registration, visit {{ContestsPage}}.
- Contests listed for Clover Kids (Gage County, Division 1): K100104 Premier Communication Contest on {{ClKPremierContest}}; K100107 Fashion Show, Purchased or Constructed Garment, on {{ClKFashionShow}}.

## Points
- Each Clover Kid exhibitor receives a Clover Kid ribbon. No premiums are printed.`},{AgeGroup:"Junior (8-10)",Source:"Nebraska 4-H Fairbook (State Fair), General Rules & Information, A. Eligibility Requirements for Exhibitors",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["4-H ages 8 to 10.","The member must be 8 before 1 January of the current year, or turn 9 during the current year."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- 4-H ages 8 to 10.
- The member must be 8 before 1 January of the current year, or turn 9 during the current year.`},{AgeGroup:"Intermediate",Source:"Nebraska 4-H Fairbook (State Fair), General Rules & Information, A. Eligibility Requirements for Exhibitors",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["4-H ages 11 to 13."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- 4-H ages 11 to 13.`},{AgeGroup:"Senior (14-18)",Source:"Nebraska 4-H Fairbook (State Fair), General Rules & Information, A. Eligibility Requirements for Exhibitors",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["4-H ages 14 to 18.","The last year of eligibility is the calendar year in which the member turns 19."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- 4-H ages 14 to 18.
- The last year of eligibility is the calendar year in which the member turns 19.`}],n=[{Title:"Project / Static Exhibit",Source:"Nebraska 4-H Fairbook (State Fair), General Rules & Information, Static Exhibits and B. Procedure for Making Entries",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["All static entries are entered by 4-H staff.","A static exhibit must have received a purple ribbon at the county fair to go on to the State Fair.","Only one entry per class per exhibitor can be made in static project areas.","Large static exhibits made for outdoors can be shown outdoors if more display space is needed inside the exhibit hall.","Static exhibits are released according to County Extension Staff unless the right papers are submitted. Dates and times are on the Master 4-H Schedule.","Static exhibit exhibitors do not receive a T-shirt."],Allowed:["Copyrighted writing, artwork, videos and images can be used in 4-H educational exhibits under Fair Use for education: use only a small amount, add new meaning, rework it into something totally different, and use it for non-profit purposes. Giving credit to the original creator is also recommended."],NotAllowed:["No firearms and no items with a blade (broad heads, knives, saws and so on) or related items of any kind. This covers real items, copies of items and item parts. Shooting sports accessories are allowed as set out in the Conservation, Wildlife and Shooting Sports Fairbook."],Judging:["Exhibits are judged against research-based standards. Purple, blue, red and white ribbons are given (see Ribbons and Placings)."],Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- All static entries are entered by 4-H staff.
- A static exhibit must have received a purple ribbon at the county fair to go on to the State Fair.
- Only one entry per class per exhibitor can be made in static project areas.
- Large static exhibits made for outdoors can be shown outdoors if more display space is needed inside the exhibit hall.
- Static exhibits are released according to County Extension Staff unless the right papers are submitted. Dates and times are on the Master 4-H Schedule.
- Static exhibit exhibitors do not receive a T-shirt.

## Allowed
- Copyrighted writing, artwork, videos and images can be used in 4-H educational exhibits under Fair Use for education: use only a small amount, add new meaning, rework it into something totally different, and use it for non-profit purposes. Giving credit to the original creator is also recommended.

## Not allowed
- No firearms and no items with a blade (broad heads, knives, saws and so on) or related items of any kind. This covers real items, copies of items and item parts. Shooting sports accessories are allowed as set out in the Conservation, Wildlife and Shooting Sports Fairbook.

## Judging
- Exhibits are judged against research-based standards. Purple, blue, red and white ribbons are given (see Ribbons and Placings).`},{Title:"Livestock Showmanship",Source:"Nebraska 4-H Fairbook (State Fair), General Rules & Information, Livestock and B. Procedure for Making Entries",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["4-H animal entries (beef, sheep, swine, goats, poultry, rabbits and dogs) are entered online by the 4-H family in ShoWorks.","An exhibitor can show up to 5 dog classes, 6 rabbits and 6 poultry entries, 6 hogs, up to 4 sheep or meat goats and up to 5 beef animals.","Protests about livestock follow the process in the State Fair General Livestock Rules & Regulations.","Smoking is not allowed in any barn."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:["Livestock entry fees (2026) are in the Fees section. For dairy cattle, see the State Fair Rules for Dairy Cattle Guidelines."]},Markdown:`## Rules
- 4-H animal entries (beef, sheep, swine, goats, poultry, rabbits and dogs) are entered online by the 4-H family in ShoWorks.
- An exhibitor can show up to 5 dog classes, 6 rabbits and 6 poultry entries, 6 hogs, up to 4 sheep or meat goats and up to 5 beef animals.
- Protests about livestock follow the process in the State Fair General Livestock Rules & Regulations.
- Smoking is not allowed in any barn.

## Notes for participants
- Livestock entry fees (2026) are in the Fees section. For dairy cattle, see the State Fair Rules for Dairy Cattle Guidelines.`},{Title:"4-H Judging Team Contest",Source:"Nebraska 4-H Fairbook (State Fair), General Rules & Information, Contests and B. Procedure for Making Entries",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Contests are entered by the family online in ShoWorks.","Only one entry per class per exhibitor can be made in a contest.","A non-refundable entry fee of {{ContestEntryFee}} is paid for all State Fair Judging Contests.","Exhibitors wear the T-shirt they are given during the presentation and the awards.","Exhibitors must not have any county identification on their clothing while they take part in contests."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Contests are entered by the family online in ShoWorks.
- Only one entry per class per exhibitor can be made in a contest.
- A non-refundable entry fee of {{ContestEntryFee}} is paid for all State Fair Judging Contests.
- Exhibitors wear the T-shirt they are given during the presentation and the awards.
- Exhibitors must not have any county identification on their clothing while they take part in contests.`}],r=JSON.parse(`[{"Title":"Project / Static Exhibit","AgeGroup":"Clover Kids NC","Source":"Gage County Fairbook, Clover Kids, Clover Kids Exhibits (Divisions 2 to 10)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Clover Kid projects are entered on {{CloverKidEntryDay1}} or {{CloverKidEntryDay2}} at the 4-H Building. Exhibits are released on {{CloverKidRelease}}.","An exhibitor is allowed ONE exhibit per class and a maximum of 10 exhibits.","Clover Kid (static) exhibits are NOT eligible for any other county competition and are NOT eligible for the State Fair.","My Choice exhibits can use any media and should relate to the project area.","Photography Display: up to three 4 inch by 6 inch photos on 11 inch by 14 inch black or white poster board. Posters or drawings: maximum size 8 1/2 inch by 11 inch.","Project descriptions are in The Big Book of 4-H Cloverbud Activities, available at the Extension Office.","Each exhibitor receives a Clover Kid ribbon.","Division 2 Science and Technology. Weather Fun: K100201 What Should I Wear Today; K100202 Rainstorm in a Jar; K100203 Make Your Own Thermometer; K100204 Weatherman Exhibit. Experimenting with the Five Senses: K100210 Rainbow & Sunset Art; K100211 Texture Rubbing. Making Air Work: K100215 Spinning Pinwheels; K100216 Balloon Rockets; K100217 Blow Painting. Good Vibrations, The Science of Sound: K100220 Kazoos; K100221 How Sound Waves Travel Poster; K100222 Making a Megaphone; K100223 Telephone; K100224 Rubber Band Guitar. The Wonder of Water: K100230 Making Flubber. Bubble Mania: K100240 Make Your Own Bubble Blower; K100241 Bubble Art. Aerospace Unit 1: K100250 Edible Rocket (build and display a rocket that can be eaten, page 4 of the manual); K100251 Paper Airplane; K100252 Rocket Picture (draw and colour a picture of your rocket and label the three main parts: fins, body tube and nose cone); K100253 Space Helmet (make and display a space helmet, page 12 of the manual). LEGO: K100260 LEGO Design.","Division 3 Community and Expressive Arts. Theatre Arts: K100305 Homemade Puppet; K100306 Story (make up a story to go with your puppet or toy to act out); K100307 Sign Language Symbols (on a poster, draw one of the American Sign Language symbols and tell what it means); K100308 Photography Display (photos of different expressions). Home Hobbies: K100310 Woodworking Exhibit; K100311 Drawing or Painting Exhibit; K100312 Beading; K100313 Cup Garden. A Space for Me: K100320 Decorative Storage Box or Container; K100321 Home Item Made From Recycled Items; K100322 Collage About Recycling or Ways to Organize Your Room; K100323 Banner; K100324 Color Poster; K100325 Seed Mosaic; K100326 Photography Display (of different textures, designs or colour combinations). Sports: K100340 Games/Sports of Different Cultures Poster; K100342 Favorite Sport Poster. Photography: K100350 Photo of an Animal; K100351 Photo of a Person; K100352 My Favorite Photo; K100353 My Best Selfie.","Division 4 Healthy Lifestyles. Fitness Is Fun: K100400 What is Physical Fitness Poster; K100401 Exercise Spinners; K100402 Baton with Streamers. Making Food for Me: K100403 Placemat (coloured and decorated; lamination or protection with clear contact paper advised); K100405 Grain Collage (neatly cut and paste pictures of grains, display in a collage); K100407 Protein Collage (neatly cut and paste pictures of protein sources and foods, display in a collage); K100408 Healthy Snack (four cookies, bars, muffins and so on, on a paper plate, or at least 1 cup of mix, for example a snack mix made from a cereal base, no-bake or simple cookie or granola bar); K100409 Photography Display (showing people cooking or eating). Making Healthy Food Choices: K100420 What's on Your Plate? Food Collage; K100422 Veggie Art Prints; K100423 Healthy Plates. Safe at Home: K100430 Fire Escape Plan (a poster or drawing of your home showing two exits, with arrows from each room showing how family members would leave in an emergency); K100431 Emergency Telephone Poster (a poster showing the different emergency phone numbers you should have posted near your telephone). Food Fun: K100440 Trail/Snack Mix; K100441 Cookie (4 on a plate); K100442 Biscuits; K100443 Decorated Cookie or Cupcake. Looking Your Best: K100450 Personalized Toothbrush; K100451 Personal Hygiene Collage; K100452 Daily Grooming Habits Chart (filled in by the exhibitor). Fall Festival, A Harvest of Fun: K100460 Seeds for Snacks; K100461 Squash Zoo Animals; K100462 Miniature Garden or Windowsill Garden; K100463 Play Dough Pumpkins.","Division 5 Environmental and Earth Science. Nature Fun: K100500 Nature Color Match Poster; K100501 Leaf Rubbings; K100502 Natural Images. The Problem of Pollution: K100510 Environmental Diorama; K100511 Create a Bumper Sticker. Helping Our Environment, Reduce, Reuse and Recycle: K100520 Making Recycled Paper; K100522 Recycled Greeting Card; K100523 Recycling Mobile. Digging Those Dinosaurs: K100530 Fossil Fun. Habitats Are Homes: K100540 Making Your Own Habitat; K100541 Making a Bird Feeder. Wildlife: K100550 Wildlife Collage; K100551 Foodchain Poster; K100552 Ecosystem Fun.","Division 6 Personal Development. My Feelings: K100600 Stress Ball Balloons; K100601 Show Your Feelings in Art. I Am Special: K100610 One of a Kind, Finger Print Investigation (a minimum of 3 different people's fingerprints); K100612 All About Me Poster; K100613 Good Things About Me Chain; K100614 Me Puppet; K100615 Name Plate. Valuing Family: K100640 Family Flower Poster; K100641 Family Album or Scrapbook; K100642 Thumbprint Family Tree. Building Character: K100650 People I Can Trust Poster; K100651 What I Want to be When I Grow Up Poster.","Division 7 Citizenship and Civic Education. Heart to Heart, Celebrating Valentine's Day with Senior Living Center Residents: K100700 Valentine Favors; K100701 Decorated Sugar Cookies; K100702 Pop-Up Valentine Cards. Food Drive, Jumping Jack-athon: K100710 Thank You Notes; K100711 Collecting Food Donations (include a copy of the pledge sheet and a photo of the food donations). Our Flag: K100720 Make Your Own Old Glory. Rules and Reasons for All Seasons: K100730 Responsibility Calendar. Our Country: K100740 Country Cut Out; K100741 USA Collage; K100742 The Bald Eagle, Our National Symbol. Democracy, Voting and You: K100750 The Statue of Liberty; K100751 Campaign Poster; K100752 Elected Officials in Our Community (create a poster highlighting one elected official in your community).","Division 8 Consumerism and Family Science. Managing Time: K100800 Paper Plate Clocks. Be Smart with Money: K100810 Needs & Wants Collage; K100811 Product Comparison Poster; K100812 Saving for a Rainy Day (make your own piggy bank). Weaving and Dying: K100840 Paper Weaving; K100841 Textile Weaving; K100842 Natural Dyed Article; K100843 Tie-Dyed Article; K100844 Dyed Article; K100845 Paper Quilt or Clothes; K100846 Clover Kid Banner. Stitch It Up: K100850 Yo-Yo Pin; K100851 Pin Cushion Jar; K100853 Stitching a Straight Line; K100854 Knots (on a 4 inch by 6 inch card, mount a knot that you have tied); K100857 Needle Book (made from the pattern using felt, found on the Gage County Extension website); K100858 Pillow (page 206 in the manual); K100859 Decorated Garment.","Division 9 Plants and Animals. Pets/Farm Animals: K100900 Create a Pet; K100901 Pet/Animal Care Kit; K100902 My Farm Animals Poster (draw a picture of one or more farm animals you have learned about through this project on 8 1/2 inch by 11 inch paper). Our Feathered Friends: K100910 Pinecone Bird Feeder; K100911 Cardinal Collage; K100912 Where They Live (make a bird nest); K100913 Feeding the Birds. Super Seed Fun: K100920 Seed Mosaic; K100921 Seed Sprouts; K100922 Fruity Prints; K100923 Leaf Collection. Art Antics: K100930 Ant ANTatomy; K100931 Ant Artists; K100932 Our Very Own Ant Farm. Bugs, Butterflies, Worms and Spiders: K100940 Bug Collection (in a jar); K100941 Egg Carton Caterpillars; K100942 Make Your Own Butterfly; K100943 Designer Bugs. Plant Science: K100950 Vegetable Grown in Your Garden (1); K100951 Flower Grown in Your Garden (1).","Division 10 Miscellaneous Exhibit: K100100 Miscellaneous Exhibit; K100102 Clover Camp/Workshop Exhibit; K100103 Exhibit completed at a 4-H Club Meeting."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Clover Kid projects are entered on {{CloverKidEntryDay1}} or {{CloverKidEntryDay2}} at the 4-H Building. Exhibits are released on {{CloverKidRelease}}.\\n- An exhibitor is allowed ONE exhibit per class and a maximum of 10 exhibits.\\n- Clover Kid (static) exhibits are NOT eligible for any other county competition and are NOT eligible for the State Fair.\\n- My Choice exhibits can use any media and should relate to the project area.\\n- Photography Display: up to three 4 inch by 6 inch photos on 11 inch by 14 inch black or white poster board. Posters or drawings: maximum size 8 1/2 inch by 11 inch.\\n- Project descriptions are in The Big Book of 4-H Cloverbud Activities, available at the Extension Office.\\n- Each exhibitor receives a Clover Kid ribbon.\\n- Division 2 Science and Technology. Weather Fun: K100201 What Should I Wear Today; K100202 Rainstorm in a Jar; K100203 Make Your Own Thermometer; K100204 Weatherman Exhibit. Experimenting with the Five Senses: K100210 Rainbow & Sunset Art; K100211 Texture Rubbing. Making Air Work: K100215 Spinning Pinwheels; K100216 Balloon Rockets; K100217 Blow Painting. Good Vibrations, The Science of Sound: K100220 Kazoos; K100221 How Sound Waves Travel Poster; K100222 Making a Megaphone; K100223 Telephone; K100224 Rubber Band Guitar. The Wonder of Water: K100230 Making Flubber. Bubble Mania: K100240 Make Your Own Bubble Blower; K100241 Bubble Art. Aerospace Unit 1: K100250 Edible Rocket (build and display a rocket that can be eaten, page 4 of the manual); K100251 Paper Airplane; K100252 Rocket Picture (draw and colour a picture of your rocket and label the three main parts: fins, body tube and nose cone); K100253 Space Helmet (make and display a space helmet, page 12 of the manual). LEGO: K100260 LEGO Design.\\n- Division 3 Community and Expressive Arts. Theatre Arts: K100305 Homemade Puppet; K100306 Story (make up a story to go with your puppet or toy to act out); K100307 Sign Language Symbols (on a poster, draw one of the American Sign Language symbols and tell what it means); K100308 Photography Display (photos of different expressions). Home Hobbies: K100310 Woodworking Exhibit; K100311 Drawing or Painting Exhibit; K100312 Beading; K100313 Cup Garden. A Space for Me: K100320 Decorative Storage Box or Container; K100321 Home Item Made From Recycled Items; K100322 Collage About Recycling or Ways to Organize Your Room; K100323 Banner; K100324 Color Poster; K100325 Seed Mosaic; K100326 Photography Display (of different textures, designs or colour combinations). Sports: K100340 Games/Sports of Different Cultures Poster; K100342 Favorite Sport Poster. Photography: K100350 Photo of an Animal; K100351 Photo of a Person; K100352 My Favorite Photo; K100353 My Best Selfie.\\n- Division 4 Healthy Lifestyles. Fitness Is Fun: K100400 What is Physical Fitness Poster; K100401 Exercise Spinners; K100402 Baton with Streamers. Making Food for Me: K100403 Placemat (coloured and decorated; lamination or protection with clear contact paper advised); K100405 Grain Collage (neatly cut and paste pictures of grains, display in a collage); K100407 Protein Collage (neatly cut and paste pictures of protein sources and foods, display in a collage); K100408 Healthy Snack (four cookies, bars, muffins and so on, on a paper plate, or at least 1 cup of mix, for example a snack mix made from a cereal base, no-bake or simple cookie or granola bar); K100409 Photography Display (showing people cooking or eating). Making Healthy Food Choices: K100420 What's on Your Plate? Food Collage; K100422 Veggie Art Prints; K100423 Healthy Plates. Safe at Home: K100430 Fire Escape Plan (a poster or drawing of your home showing two exits, with arrows from each room showing how family members would leave in an emergency); K100431 Emergency Telephone Poster (a poster showing the different emergency phone numbers you should have posted near your telephone). Food Fun: K100440 Trail/Snack Mix; K100441 Cookie (4 on a plate); K100442 Biscuits; K100443 Decorated Cookie or Cupcake. Looking Your Best: K100450 Personalized Toothbrush; K100451 Personal Hygiene Collage; K100452 Daily Grooming Habits Chart (filled in by the exhibitor). Fall Festival, A Harvest of Fun: K100460 Seeds for Snacks; K100461 Squash Zoo Animals; K100462 Miniature Garden or Windowsill Garden; K100463 Play Dough Pumpkins.\\n- Division 5 Environmental and Earth Science. Nature Fun: K100500 Nature Color Match Poster; K100501 Leaf Rubbings; K100502 Natural Images. The Problem of Pollution: K100510 Environmental Diorama; K100511 Create a Bumper Sticker. Helping Our Environment, Reduce, Reuse and Recycle: K100520 Making Recycled Paper; K100522 Recycled Greeting Card; K100523 Recycling Mobile. Digging Those Dinosaurs: K100530 Fossil Fun. Habitats Are Homes: K100540 Making Your Own Habitat; K100541 Making a Bird Feeder. Wildlife: K100550 Wildlife Collage; K100551 Foodchain Poster; K100552 Ecosystem Fun.\\n- Division 6 Personal Development. My Feelings: K100600 Stress Ball Balloons; K100601 Show Your Feelings in Art. I Am Special: K100610 One of a Kind, Finger Print Investigation (a minimum of 3 different people's fingerprints); K100612 All About Me Poster; K100613 Good Things About Me Chain; K100614 Me Puppet; K100615 Name Plate. Valuing Family: K100640 Family Flower Poster; K100641 Family Album or Scrapbook; K100642 Thumbprint Family Tree. Building Character: K100650 People I Can Trust Poster; K100651 What I Want to be When I Grow Up Poster.\\n- Division 7 Citizenship and Civic Education. Heart to Heart, Celebrating Valentine's Day with Senior Living Center Residents: K100700 Valentine Favors; K100701 Decorated Sugar Cookies; K100702 Pop-Up Valentine Cards. Food Drive, Jumping Jack-athon: K100710 Thank You Notes; K100711 Collecting Food Donations (include a copy of the pledge sheet and a photo of the food donations). Our Flag: K100720 Make Your Own Old Glory. Rules and Reasons for All Seasons: K100730 Responsibility Calendar. Our Country: K100740 Country Cut Out; K100741 USA Collage; K100742 The Bald Eagle, Our National Symbol. Democracy, Voting and You: K100750 The Statue of Liberty; K100751 Campaign Poster; K100752 Elected Officials in Our Community (create a poster highlighting one elected official in your community).\\n- Division 8 Consumerism and Family Science. Managing Time: K100800 Paper Plate Clocks. Be Smart with Money: K100810 Needs & Wants Collage; K100811 Product Comparison Poster; K100812 Saving for a Rainy Day (make your own piggy bank). Weaving and Dying: K100840 Paper Weaving; K100841 Textile Weaving; K100842 Natural Dyed Article; K100843 Tie-Dyed Article; K100844 Dyed Article; K100845 Paper Quilt or Clothes; K100846 Clover Kid Banner. Stitch It Up: K100850 Yo-Yo Pin; K100851 Pin Cushion Jar; K100853 Stitching a Straight Line; K100854 Knots (on a 4 inch by 6 inch card, mount a knot that you have tied); K100857 Needle Book (made from the pattern using felt, found on the Gage County Extension website); K100858 Pillow (page 206 in the manual); K100859 Decorated Garment.\\n- Division 9 Plants and Animals. Pets/Farm Animals: K100900 Create a Pet; K100901 Pet/Animal Care Kit; K100902 My Farm Animals Poster (draw a picture of one or more farm animals you have learned about through this project on 8 1/2 inch by 11 inch paper). Our Feathered Friends: K100910 Pinecone Bird Feeder; K100911 Cardinal Collage; K100912 Where They Live (make a bird nest); K100913 Feeding the Birds. Super Seed Fun: K100920 Seed Mosaic; K100921 Seed Sprouts; K100922 Fruity Prints; K100923 Leaf Collection. Art Antics: K100930 Ant ANTatomy; K100931 Ant Artists; K100932 Our Very Own Ant Farm. Bugs, Butterflies, Worms and Spiders: K100940 Bug Collection (in a jar); K100941 Egg Carton Caterpillars; K100942 Make Your Own Butterfly; K100943 Designer Bugs. Plant Science: K100950 Vegetable Grown in Your Garden (1); K100951 Flower Grown in Your Garden (1).\\n- Division 10 Miscellaneous Exhibit: K100100 Miscellaneous Exhibit; K100102 Clover Camp/Workshop Exhibit; K100103 Exhibit completed at a 4-H Club Meeting."},{"Title":"Livestock Showmanship","AgeGroup":"Clover Kids NC","Source":"Gage County Fairbook, Clover Kids, Livestock Show and Rabbit & Poultry Show","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Clover Kids shows (Gage County): {{CloverKidShowDates}}.","Location: {{CloverKidShowLocations}}."],"Rules":["Youth must be enrolled in 4hOnline by {{EnrollmentDeadline}}. All Clover Kid livestock must be entered online by {{CloverKidLivestockDeadline}}.","Owning livestock is not required. A Clover Kid can use livestock from a 4-H member that is already on the grounds. The Clover Kid must say whose animal they use, or say they are bringing their own.","Minimal stalling is available. Livestock that comes on the day of the show must leave on the day of the show. There is no overnight stalling.","There is no pre-identification and no YQCA is needed to take part.","The show is non-competitive. Every Clover Kid receives the same award and a free show shirt.","Livestock is weighed. Under 4-H policy, livestock must weigh under 350 lbs.","Clover Kids can show as many species as they want. The show is a blow-and-go only.","Clover Kids can also take part in PeeWee Showmanship, open class, and the Clover Kid Livestock Show.","Age: 5 to 7 years old as of 1 January 2026.","Livestock show: hogs, beef cattle, dairy cattle, dairy goats, meat goats and sheep are checked in and weighed by Extension Staff. Animals must be under 350 lbs. Maximum entries per exhibitor: 1 hog, 1 beef calf, 1 dairy calf, 1 dairy goat, 1 meat goat and 1 sheep. Show order: hogs, beef, cattle, dairy cattle, dairy goats, meat goats and sheep.","Rabbit and poultry show: Clover Kids take part during the respective species shows. Check-in is 30 minutes before the show (broiler, poultry, rabbit). Broilers, poultry and rabbits are checked in by Extension Staff. Maximum entries per exhibitor: 1 broiler, 1 poultry and 1 rabbit.","More information: {{CloverKidLivestockInfo}}."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Clover Kids shows (Gage County): {{CloverKidShowDates}}.\\n- Location: {{CloverKidShowLocations}}.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Youth must be enrolled in 4hOnline by {{EnrollmentDeadline}}. All Clover Kid livestock must be entered online by {{CloverKidLivestockDeadline}}.\\n- Owning livestock is not required. A Clover Kid can use livestock from a 4-H member that is already on the grounds. The Clover Kid must say whose animal they use, or say they are bringing their own.\\n- Minimal stalling is available. Livestock that comes on the day of the show must leave on the day of the show. There is no overnight stalling.\\n- There is no pre-identification and no YQCA is needed to take part.\\n- The show is non-competitive. Every Clover Kid receives the same award and a free show shirt.\\n- Livestock is weighed. Under 4-H policy, livestock must weigh under 350 lbs.\\n- Clover Kids can show as many species as they want. The show is a blow-and-go only.\\n- Clover Kids can also take part in PeeWee Showmanship, open class, and the Clover Kid Livestock Show.\\n- Age: 5 to 7 years old as of 1 January 2026.\\n- Livestock show: hogs, beef cattle, dairy cattle, dairy goats, meat goats and sheep are checked in and weighed by Extension Staff. Animals must be under 350 lbs. Maximum entries per exhibitor: 1 hog, 1 beef calf, 1 dairy calf, 1 dairy goat, 1 meat goat and 1 sheep. Show order: hogs, beef, cattle, dairy cattle, dairy goats, meat goats and sheep.\\n- Rabbit and poultry show: Clover Kids take part during the respective species shows. Check-in is 30 minutes before the show (broiler, poultry, rabbit). Broilers, poultry and rabbits are checked in by Extension Staff. Maximum entries per exhibitor: 1 broiler, 1 poultry and 1 rabbit.\\n- More information: {{CloverKidLivestockInfo}}."}]`),s=[{Key:"EnrollmentDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"4-H enrolment deadline",Value:"June 15 of the current year",Source:"Nebraska 4-H Fairbook (State Fair), General Rules & Information A; Gage County Fairbook, Clover Kids"},{Key:"EnrollmentWebsite",Kind:"link",Label:"4-H enrolment website (4hOnline)",Value:"http://v2.4honline.com",Source:"Gage County Fairbook, Clover Kids"},{Key:"StateEntryDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"State Fair entry deadline (animals, in-person events, contests)",Value:"August 10, 8 PM central time",Source:"Nebraska 4-H Fairbook (State Fair), General Rules & Information B. Procedure for Making Entries"},{Key:"ContestEntryFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Contest entry fee",Value:"$5.00 per person, non-refundable",Source:"Nebraska 4-H Fairbook (State Fair), General Rules & Information, Contests: Contest Entry Fees"},{Key:"LivestockEntryFees",Kind:"fee",Label:"2026 livestock entry fees",Value:"Market Beef, Breeding Beef, Feeder Calf: $50. Dairy Cattle: see the State Fair Rules for Dairy Cattle Guidelines. Meat Goats, Market Lambs, Market Swine: $22.50. Breeding Sheep, Breeding Does, Breeding Gilts: $22.50. Dogs: $5.00 per entry (Obedience, Agility, Rally, Skillathon). Poultry and Rabbits: $5.00 per entry. All livestock entry fees are non-refundable.",Source:"Nebraska 4-H Fairbook (State Fair), General Rules & Information, Livestock 1"},{Key:"StateFairVenue",Kind:"address",Label:"Nebraska State Fair venue",Value:{Name:"Nebraska State Fair, State Fair Park (4-H/FFA Exhibit building)",Address:"",City:"",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"Nebraska 4-H Fairbook (State Fair), General Rules & Information, On Grounds"},{Key:"CountyVenue",Kind:"address",Label:"Gage County Clover Kids venue",Value:{Name:"4-H Building, Gage County Fairgrounds (Main Livestock Barn Show Arena for livestock; Poultry/Rabbit Complex for rabbits and poultry)",Address:"",City:"",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"Gage County Fairbook, Clover Kids"},{Key:"CloverKidEntryDay1",Kind:"date",Label:"Clover Kids static entry, day 1",Value:"Monday, July 20 (2026), 5:00 pm to 8:00 pm, 4-H Building",Source:"Gage County Fairbook, Clover Kids"},{Key:"CloverKidEntryDay2",Kind:"date",Label:"Clover Kids static entry, day 2",Value:"Tuesday, July 21 (2026), 10:00 am to 2:00 pm, 4-H Building",Source:"Gage County Fairbook, Clover Kids"},{Key:"CloverKidRelease",Kind:"date",Label:"Clover Kids exhibit release",Value:"Sunday, July 26 (2026), 7:00 pm",Source:"Gage County Fairbook, Clover Kids"},{Key:"CloverKidLivestockDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Clover Kids livestock, rabbit and poultry online entry deadline",Value:"July 15 (2026), 5:00 p.m. at gage.fairwire.com",Source:"Gage County Fairbook, Clover Kids"},{Key:"CloverKidFashionDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Clover Kids fashion show registration deadline",Value:"July 8 (paper registration form at the Extension Office)",Source:"Gage County Fairbook, Clover Kids, Contests Division 1"},{Key:"ClKPremierContest",Kind:"text",Label:"Premier Communication Contest (Clover Kids)",Value:"April 12, Gage County Extension Office (class K100104)",Source:"Gage County Fairbook, Clover Kids, Contests Division 1"},{Key:"ClKFashionShow",Kind:"text",Label:"Fashion Show, Purchased or Constructed Garment (Clover Kids)",Value:"July 12, 4-H Building, Gage County Fairgrounds. Registration deadline July 8 (class K100107)",Source:"Gage County Fairbook, Clover Kids, Contests Division 1"},{Key:"CloverKidShowDates",Kind:"text",Label:"Clover Kids shows",Value:"Broiler Show: Wednesday, July 22, 4:30 p.m. Poultry Show: Friday, July 24, 1:30 p.m. Rabbit Show: Saturday, July 25, 9:30 a.m. Livestock show: Saturday, July 25, check-in and show 11:30 a.m. to 12:30 p.m.",Source:"Gage County Fairbook, Clover Kids, Rabbit & Poultry Show and Livestock Show"},{Key:"CloverKidShowLocations",Kind:"text",Label:"Clover Kids show locations",Value:"Poultry/Rabbit Complex for rabbits and poultry; Main Livestock Barn Show Arena for livestock",Source:"Gage County Fairbook, Clover Kids"},{Key:"CloverKidContests",Kind:"text",Label:"Clover Kids contests (Gage County)",Value:"Premier Communication Contest, April 12, Gage County Extension Office. Fashion Show, Purchased or Constructed Garment, July 12, 4-H Building, Gage County Fairgrounds, registration deadline July 8.",Source:"Gage County Fairbook, Clover Kids, Contests Division 1"},{Key:"CloverKidLivestockInfo",Kind:"link",Label:"More about the Clover Kid livestock show",Value:"go.unl.edu/gagecloverkidlivestock",Source:"Gage County Fairbook, Clover Kids"},{Key:"GageFairWebsite",Kind:"link",Label:"Gage County Fair (Open Class Fairbook)",Value:"gagecountyfair.com",Source:"Gage County Fairbook, Clover Kids"},{Key:"ManagementTeam",Kind:"text",Label:"2025-2026 Nebraska 4-H State Fair Management Team",Value:"Jill Goedeken, Brandy Schulze, Angela Abts, Kimberly Cook, Calvin DeVries, Jennifer Epp, Kristin Geisert, Nicholas Hoag, Cole Meador, Darci Pesek",Source:"Nebraska 4-H Fairbook home page, General Rules & Information"},{Key:"ContestsPage",Kind:"link",Label:"County contest registration page",Value:"https://extension.unl.edu/statewide/gage/4-h/gage-county-fair/",Source:"Gage County Fairbook, Clover Kids, Contests Division 1"}],l=[{Claim:"The eligibility, entry procedure, protest rules, ribbon meanings, entry fees, static, contest, livestock and on-grounds rules written here are those of the 2026 Nebraska 4-H Fairbook (State Fair), General Rules & Information page.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"Nebraska 4-H Fairbook (State Fair), General Rules & Information",Url:"https://4h.unl.edu/4-h-fairbook-nebraska-state-fair/general-rules-information/"},{Claim:"The Clover Kids rules, class list, dates, shows and contests are those of the Gage County (Nebraska) Fairbook Clover Kids page for 2026. They are one county's edition.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"Gage County Fairbook, Clover Kids",Url:"https://extension.unl.edu/gage-county-fairbook/clover-kids/"},{Claim:"The two pages print no Champion or Reserve Champion rule, no bonus points, no marks for Public Speaking or Demonstration, no rules for the Judging Team Contest itself, no State Fair venue address and no contact phone or e-mail. These stay empty on purpose. Nothing was written from general knowledge.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"Nebraska 4-H Fairbook (State Fair), General Rules & Information",Url:"https://4h.unl.edu/4-h-fairbook-nebraska-state-fair/general-rules-information/"}],h={TemplateKey:e,Year:2026,Note:t,Page:o,ParticipantTypes:a,AgeGroups:i,Competitions:n,CompetitionAgeGroups:r,Variables:s,Evidence:l};export{i as AgeGroups,r as CompetitionAgeGroups,n as Competitions,l as Evidence,t as Note,o as Page,a as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,s as Variables,d as Year,h as default};
